      "message": "Bounds and genid are const and computed upfront for `SkPathData`, but we still have a lazy compute path for convexity.  While it\u0027s not unsafe to race on convexity, it can be suboptimal (multiple threads computing convexity in parallel), so there\u0027s a case to be made for keeping `PreCachedPath` around and priming convexity instead.\n\nBut it\u0027s unclear that multi-threaded/parallel consumers is what we should be optimizing for at this level, plus we don\u0027t currently do that -- so I\u0027m inclined to drop the helper completely for now and revisit in the future if needed.",
